{"name":"Blooming Aster","hex":"#d7e2ee","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blooming","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of bloom"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Opening in blossoms; flowering.","Thriving in health, beauty, and vigor, vigour; indicating the freshness and beauties of youth or health."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blooming"},{"term":"aster","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several plants of the genus Aster; one of its flowers.","A star-shaped structure formed during the mitosis of a cell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aster"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aster (genus)","blocks":[{"text":"Aster is a genus of perennial flowering plants in the family Asteraceae. Its circumscription has been narrowed, and it now encompasses around 170 species, all but one of which are restricted to Eurasia; many species formerly in Aster are now in other genera of the tribe Astereae. Aster amellus is the type species of the genus and the family Asteraceae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Asteraceae_-_Aster_amellus.JPG/330px-Asteraceae_-_Aster_amellus.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aster_(genus)","wikidata":"Q517130"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Aster_flower.jpg/500px-Aster_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Aster_flower.jpg/1280px-Aster_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Aster_flower.jpg/500px-Aster_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Multi layer petals Aster flower","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAster_flower.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Aster-alpinus.JPG/500px-Aster-alpinus.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Aster-alpinus.JPG/500px-Aster-alpinus.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aster alpinus is the only species of Aster (sensu stricto) that is native to North America; it is found in mountains across the Northern Hemisphere.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAster-alpinus.JPG"}],"sounds":{"blooming":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f2/En-us-blooming.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/f2/En-us-blooming.ogg/En-us-blooming.ogg.mp3"}],"aster":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1c/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-aster.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/1/1c/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-aster.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-aster.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/1/1c/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-aster.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-aster.wav.ogg"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Vick's aster book for florists (1915) (14778041852)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Vick%27s_aster_book_for_florists_%281915%29_%2814778041852%29.jpg/500px-Vick%27s_aster_book_for_florists_%281915%29_%2814778041852%29.jpg","ratio":1.3637489677952106,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vick%27s_aster_book_for_florists_(1915)_(14778041852).jpg","share":0.36875},{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.